title: Authorizations › Case page › Where the worklist and the case page lead
route: /authorizations
intro: Every click that takes a person from the Authorizations worklist or a case page into another part of the product. What the case page writes to other screens is in the next diagram.
dir: LR
also: The row buttons of the worklist (Go to action, Send to payer, Open on Dashboard, Open the denial, the review buttons, Start reauthorization) are drawn in their own diagrams; this one shows the links that leave the module from the page itself and from a case page.
---
screen q "Authorizations worklist"
screen cp "A case page (any tab)"

click l1 "Click 'New Case'"
click l2 "Click the 'Coverage needs a fix' pill on a row"
click l6 "With the payer view: click '4 sent today'"
click l3 "On the coverage card: click 'Open Eligibility & Benefits'"
click l4 "On a denied request: click 'Open in Denial Intelligence'\n(in the 'Next:' block)"
click l5 "Click 'Open in review and sign' or 'Send to payer'\n('Send to payer' is the 'Next:' block's button once every check passes)"
click l7 "Click 'Back to Authorizations' or the 'Authorizations' crumb"
click l9 "In a request's quick view panel: click 'Review and sign'\n(shown while the request is being prepared)"
click l10 "On the card for a case at another site: click 'Back to the Dashboard'"
click l8 "Click 'Open on the Dashboard'\n(in the 'Next:' block or next to the status line, once the request is past Preparing)"

goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › How a case starts and resumes"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Verify › Ways in and pre-fill"
goto g5 "Continues in: Dashboard › Lifecycle › Click a state to filter the table"
goto g3 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › A denial opened"
goto g4 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › Send to payer and review and sign"
goto g6 "Continues in: Authorizations › Worklist › Arrive and read the views"
goto g7 "Continues in: Dashboard › Request drawer › Open and read a request"
goto g8 "Continues in: Dashboard › Arrive › What the page shows"

q --> l1 --> g1
q --> l2 --> g2
q --> l6 --> g5
q --> l9 --> g4
q --> l10 --> g8
cp --> l3 --> g2
cp --> l4 --> g3
cp --> l5 --> g4
cp --> l7 --> g6
cp --> l8 --> g7
